Z||000009||gabriel||03-05-2001||06:36 AM||||&gt;My drivers side seat rails are frozen<P>  Maybe not.<P>I had similar problems.  What happens is that thin spring that connects the release lever to the other side rusts out & that side can't engage it's release lever. (both tracks have a locking thingy)<P>  You need to pry that lever (it's not too easy to find) outward with a screwdriver & then that side stays free to move.<P>   I hope that helps.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Wolfhound||03-05-2001||06:56 AM||||Thanks Gabriel, That makes sense, cause the lever moves, I,ll check that first thing this morning.<P>FieroJoe, For some reason the power mirrows were in the trunk?<p>[This message has been edited by Wolfhound (edited 03-05-2001).]||||reg||14
Z||000011||RRobinson||03-05-2001||11:39 AM||||Hey Wolfhound,<BR>Good pictures. I'm in the middle of a similar mini-restoration on an 87 SE V6 5-speed. Granted, mine has a few more miles (177,000Kms) on it, and didn't have any plants growing through it, but it was a similar cosmetic mess. It had the following "lowlights":<BR>- 4 holes where the wing used to be- one broken wing stand in the trunk.<BR>- Destroyed seats<BR>- No horn paddles on the steering wheel<BR>- Totally shotgunned paint on the front bumper- the worst I've ever seen.<BR>- All the clearcoat was peeling off the hood.<BR>- Awful discount stereo, only one speaker worked and the antenna was missing and mount broken off.<BR>- Proper wheels missing. P185/75 tires on black 14 inch steel wheels.<BR>- Horrible tan/grey/black aftermarket graphics on sides. Took 4 hours with a heat gun to get them off. Many curse words involved. <BR>- many more broken/missing parts.<P>  Now the good news: Mechanically, it seems solid, and after my usual new-Fiero tune-up (Oil, coolant, tranny fluids plus plugs, wires, cap & rotor, and air filter), as well as a new dog-bone, it's running really good. Most of the other problems have been adressed as well, with a new wing, a hood and bumper repaint, GT wheels and tires, decent seats, a good steering wheel, and a good OEM cass player and antenna. Most of this stuff I already had on hand so it didn't cost much. Next up: I'm refinishing a set of high tech wheels, and I'll need 14" tires, and It also needs a windshield. Anyways, good luck with your 86 SE, I love seeing a Fiero saved from the boneyard.<P>Ryan <BR>  ||||reg||10
